		<title>Teen&#039;s AI-guided mountain hike ends with a helicopter rescue and a lesson in common sense</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/teens-ai-guided-mountain-hike-ends-with-a-helicopter-rescue-and-a-lesson-in-common-sense/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/teens-ai-guided-mountain-hike-ends-with-a-helicopter-rescue-and-a-lesson-in-common-sense/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Manuel Uth]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2026 09:57:42 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI in practice]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Short News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Anthropic]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Claude]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=41242</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/claude_hiking.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        A 16-year-old planned his hiking route on Crown Mountain near Vancouver using Anthropic's Claude and had to be airlifted off a steep rock face. The chatbot had sent him down a route that requires climbing gear. Bryce doesn't blame the AI but says he'll never use it for route planning again.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/teens-ai-guided-mountain-hike-ends-with-a-helicopter-rescue-and-a-lesson-in-common-sense/">Teen&#039;s AI-guided mountain hike ends with a helicopter rescue and a lesson in common sense</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
