		<title>ChatGPT rated &quot;unacceptable risk&quot; for teens after parental alerts failed during suicide conversations</title>
		<link>https://the-decoder.com/chatgpt-rated-unacceptable-risk-for-teens-after-parental-alerts-failed-during-suicide-conversations/</link>
					<comments>https://the-decoder.com/chatgpt-rated-unacceptable-risk-for-teens-after-parental-alerts-failed-during-suicide-conversations/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Manuel Uth]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Wed, 07 Oct 2026 12:34:34 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[AI and society]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI and safety]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[ChatGPT]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[OpenAI]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://the-decoder.com/?p=41204</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p><img width="1376" height="768" src="https://the-decoder.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/chatgpt_safety_fail.png" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="" style="height: auto; margin-bottom: 10px;" decoding="async" /></p>
<p>        OpenAI's teen safety features for ChatGPT failed an independent audit. After more than 4,000 test prompts, the Common Sense Media Youth AI Safety Institute rated the service an "unacceptable risk" for minors. Conversations about suicide and self-harm on test accounts never triggered a parental alert. The institute wants teenagers locked out until safety can be independently verified.</p>
<p>The article <a href="https://the-decoder.com/chatgpt-rated-unacceptable-risk-for-teens-after-parental-alerts-failed-during-suicide-conversations/">ChatGPT rated &quot;unacceptable risk&quot; for teens after parental alerts failed during suicide conversations</a> appeared first on <a href="https://the-decoder.com">The Decoder</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
